::PC_U02_L07_GP_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U02_L07_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.TR.6
Question:
A student solves a one-variable trigonometric ratio problem. Which step best supports a valid solution for item.
{
=A. Identify the trig ratio, substitute known values, solve, and check the angle or side in context#Correct. This answer follows the lesson concept and connects the result to the stated standard.
~B. Choose a ratio after solving so the answer matches#This choice uses a related idea but does not complete the required reasoning for the stated standard.
~C. Use any trig ratio because all ratios produce the same value#This choice reflects a common misconception or an incomplete step.
~D. Report the calculator output without checking units or context#This choice does not match the conditions in the question.\}

